From 0c42340b88ab19437d0d11d14fe196e4f36f97b9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arthur Sonzogni <arthursonzogni@chromium.org>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 10:21:56 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [M156] Don't leak cross-origin URLs in COEP and COOP reports

Original change's description:
> Don't leak cross-origin URLs in COEP and COOP reports
>
> COEP reports sent to a parent included the full initial URL of the
> child navigation, assuming the parent chose it. That doesn't hold for
> history navigations (the stored URL may be a cross-origin post-redirect
> URL) or navigations started by a cross-origin child. Similarly, COOP
> reports exposed nextResponseURL on history traversals.
>
> Only report the full URL if a document same-origin with the parent
> supplied it. Don't treat history, restore and reload navigations as COOP
> navigation sources.
>
> Fixed: 572310924
> Change-Id: I030d9618db5175ffc16a26c46a057d16515f256d
> Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8783654
> Commit-Queue: Arthur Sonzogni <arthursonzogni@chromium.org>
> Reviewed-by: Camille Lamy <clamy@chromium.org>
